<title>USA: CardioThoracic backs Street projections.</title>
<headline>CardioThoracic backs Street projections.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>CardioThoracic Systems Inc is comfortable with analysts' projections of a loss of $1.48 per share this year and a loss of $1.38 per share next year, said chief executive Richard Ferrari in an interview.</p>
<p>The surgical devices maker went public this spring.</p>
<p>Chief financial officer Steve Van Dick said, &quot;We'll reach breakeven in mid- to early-1998, with just a slight profit. I don't expect we will end 1997 in the black.&quot;  The Cupertino, Calif.-based company is developing equipment that permits surgeons to operate on the heart while it is still beating and without making a massive chest incision.</p>
</text>
